    "updated_at": "2022-09-13T12:00:41Z",
    "body": "I had a very similar question over in the Q/A [here](https://github.com/starship/starship/discussions/4363).\r\n\r\n#1891 would be great and solve most of my issues, however I did notice another bug/possible enhancement. The `directory` module should not attempt a `git` status check if you already have either disabled the `git_` modules or especially if you have `truncate_to_repo = false`. See [source](https://github.com/starship/starship/blob/master/src/modules/directory.rs#L53).\r\n\r\nThis appears to be why the `directory` call takes a full second in a large network directory I often work inside.",
